    "description": "/// Drives four dedicated CustomTwoBoneIK chains (both hands, both feet) toward ledge pins WITHOUT /// fighting the animation. /// /// Every LateUpdate (before the IK solvers run, so the bones still hold the pure animation pose): /// 1. read the animated end bone (hand / foot) and convert it to ledge space /// x = along the ledge (side) y = up z = into the wall (forward) /// 2. measure its velocity in that space /// 3. per axis, influence = follow[axis] * |velocity[axis]| / ikVelocityRef /// still limb -> target = pin (locked to the ledge) /// moving limb -> target slides toward the animated position on the axes that are moving /// 4. rotation follows the animation by rotationFollow * movement /// 5. position / rotation weights lerp from the Idle values to the Move values with movement /// /// Setup: put this on an object under the player ROOT (NOT under the Animator/model, so /// PlayerAnimInstance.GetComponentInChildren&lt;CustomTwoBoneIK&gt;() never finds these). Assign the four chains. /// Feet are optional; leave empty for hands only. ///",
